From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Palgunov <toxblh@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:26:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 90/99] v8: e2k: open the window of V8 code with nfx = 0

The registers of e2k-v5 are 128 bits wide.  With setwd ... nfx = 1 the
high halves of the registers of the window are now and then lost when it
is spilled (on an interrupt or a deep call): the layer test of 128-bit
values (v8-e2k-lab simd/test_lsx) gives 11-15 wrong results in 304 800
checks per run with nfx = 1, on random instructions, and none in five runs
with nfx = 0.  Code that keeps only 64-bit values is not affected, wasm
SIMD is.  No cost measured: bench.js on 8SV is the same with both (within
1 %).
---
 chromium/v8/src/codegen/e2k/la_asm.h | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chromium/v8/src/codegen/e2k/la_asm.h b/chromium/v8/src/codegen/e2k/la_asm.h
index 4bbadda06b..b5ce37ed0b 100644
--- a/chromium/v8/src/codegen/e2k/la_asm.h
+++ b/chromium/v8/src/codegen/e2k/la_asm.h
@@ -217,7 +217,11 @@ class Assembler : private e2k::Assembler {
   void enter(int nargs) {
     assert(nargs >= 0 && nargs <= 8);
     Own own(this);
-    C(setwd(kWindow); setbn(5, 32, 0));
+    // nfx = 0: the window is spilled with the high halves of the registers
+    // (128 bits on e2k-v5); with nfx = 1 a spill on an interrupt or a deep
+    // call now and then loses them (v8-e2k-lab simd/test_lsx: 11-15 wrong
+    // results in 304 800 with nfx = 1, none with nfx = 0).
+    C(setwd(kWindow, false); setbn(5, 32, 0));
     C(for (int i = 4; i < 8; i++) addd(i - 4, i < nargs ? Src1(e2k::r(i)) : Src1(0), 0, e2k::r(4 + i)));
     C(for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) addd(i, i < nargs ? Src1(e2k::r(i)) : Src1(0), 0, e2k::r(4 + i)));
     Reg rest[59]; int n = 0;
